[{:db/id "q-5985/selection/3af4c9872ff1520d393ee6cedb30b1f871eadf542d020998d03fef3b33cc9b80" :answer/id #uuid "2900ee99-267d-5ede-851f-464024e478be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{5}{3}{x}^{3}+\\frac{11}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-5985/selection/2fd62fea493240af2ec6c0c031784796b397f00b9da7e74020dafc5479c5f007" :answer/id #uuid "199910d0-a546-5dbf-8303-d453dd3a05b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=5{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-5985/selection/9dc1a248c1a269f1fed9fe2b8d18b5c10c7917aa26843da253dce5a818fd69c2" :answer/id #uuid "59128ef1-2e85-565b-b109-06722de7a1d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=10x-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-5985/selection/ca488b4011fd109c73bb8f0c5c1f0226bb11cf37e6101f41210f3eb44e1e269d" :answer/id #uuid "761083cb-de89-58d8-b1dd-f3a75f56f9be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{5}{3}{x}^{3}+x+\\frac{12}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-5985/selection/ae9aa5d4302a577a2b4d810c17262cb1dc685af569385e6fd354fb3e505c78cb" :answer/id #uuid "0364b99a-2a69-50fb-a319-287a64ee583d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=5{x}^{5}+\\frac{9}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-5985/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f44ccde7-5000-5d85-98d7-850418ec4789" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-5985/selection/3af4c9872ff1520d393ee6cedb30b1f871eadf542d020998d03fef3b33cc9b80" :answer-field/choices ["q-5985/selection/3af4c9872ff1520d393ee6cedb30b1f871eadf542d020998d03fef3b33cc9b80" "q-5985/selection/2fd62fea493240af2ec6c0c031784796b397f00b9da7e74020dafc5479c5f007" "q-5985/selection/9dc1a248c1a269f1fed9fe2b8d18b5c10c7917aa26843da253dce5a818fd69c2" "q-5985/selection/ca488b4011fd109c73bb8f0c5c1f0226bb11cf37e6101f41210f3eb44e1e269d" "q-5985/selection/ae9aa5d4302a577a2b4d810c17262cb1dc685af569385e6fd354fb3e505c78cb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-5985" :question/id #uuid "0027455e-0f8d-5d58-b3c8-8d6a1a10e5aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-5985" :question/problem "The length of a curve $y=f(x)$ is given by ${\\int }_{3}^{5}\\sqrt{1+25{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Which of the following could be  an equation for this curve?" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe're given that \n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{3}^{5}\\sqrt{1+25{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nComparing the above with the arc length formula, we see that we must have\n\n$$\n[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}=25{x}^{4}\\,⟹\\,{f}^{′}(x)=\\pm 5{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIntegrating the above equation with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\pm 5\\int {x}^{2}\\text{ d}x \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{5}{3}{x}^{3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, the only one that has the required form is $y=-\\frac{5}{3}{x}^{3}+\\frac{11}{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-5985/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55f783c4-25d6-5855-877e-31bed16b12c4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-5985"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-120752/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" :answer/id #uuid "3e2a4a79-7a3d-55dc-bcf4-51cc36694ee4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120752/selection/76c690f03fbd5162fa21765f31a2046fdb1ba896a35e9b165f53f25a86cd1745" :answer/id #uuid "2d1cf6b6-b159-5195-b5f1-20fb75d0909c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120752/selection/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555" :answer/id #uuid "e4dd42c4-9e1e-5eb7-a24b-f692baad9428" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120752/selection/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" :answer/id #uuid "2d75a79b-c2ab-54a7-a612-1d1ae36826c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120752/selection/8a135ace4937b1ffa2c52fbce040999428005f5395e9d793e225144a0384a1ba" :answer/id #uuid "f9de82a6-c58a-5cd8-93a6-d752714441c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120752/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "246db429-8625-5142-b366-da5557858029" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-120752/selection/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" :answer-field/choices ["q-120752/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" "q-120752/selection/76c690f03fbd5162fa21765f31a2046fdb1ba896a35e9b165f53f25a86cd1745" "q-120752/selection/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555" "q-120752/selection/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" "q-120752/selection/8a135ace4937b1ffa2c52fbce040999428005f5395e9d793e225144a0384a1ba"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-120752" :question/id #uuid "4437946f-3374-5e77-9f64-df37a3956524" :question/math-academy-id "q-120752" :question/problem "Compute the arc length of $y=\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}$ for $x\\in [\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},1].$" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}},$ $a=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ and $b=1.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}} & =\\sqrt{1+{(-\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{1-{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1-{x}^{2}+{x}^{2}}{1-{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}$ to the formula for the arc length, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}/2}^{1}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}/2}^{1}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x){|}_{\\sqrt{2}/2}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-120752/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f87bc14d-5e68-5a5e-bec8-f1b5b21c02e8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-120752"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122287/selection/a84d639d380e10cb74c92005685f9f65779377dfb51342c280c63c645679bbea" :answer/id #uuid "3de33f0b-6fbd-5284-a6a7-464996ab991e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122287/selection/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" :answer/id #uuid "ef101227-9347-5b0f-887a-58c6b7c4a2d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122287/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" :answer/id #uuid "2009f87b-8f15-570f-9bda-1b41c9aee810" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122287/selection/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c" :answer/id #uuid "2cfdb7c3-fb14-545a-84b4-cc17cf2352b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122287/selection/801bcdd9cb6a10cec998162e05f71050c8aaf0c6974f095bdcaef715a09f4aee" :answer/id #uuid "aabfc78e-66e6-5edf-820f-dd3ddd4bbfe6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122287/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "16ea3d48-f723-5f62-8215-c2767ccc9abc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122287/selection/801bcdd9cb6a10cec998162e05f71050c8aaf0c6974f095bdcaef715a09f4aee" :answer-field/choices ["q-122287/selection/a84d639d380e10cb74c92005685f9f65779377dfb51342c280c63c645679bbea" "q-122287/selection/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" "q-122287/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" "q-122287/selection/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c" "q-122287/selection/801bcdd9cb6a10cec998162e05f71050c8aaf0c6974f095bdcaef715a09f4aee"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122287" :question/id #uuid "68cf6bb9-4815-5cbd-af07-6f1b5adb668a" :question/math-academy-id "q-122287" :question/problem "Compute the arc length of $y=\\frac{2}{3}{(1+{x}^{2})}^{3/2}$ for $x\\in [0,3].$" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=\\frac{2}{3}{(1+{x}^{2})}^{3/2},$ $a=0,$ and $b=3.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}{(1+{x}^{2})}^{1/2}\\cdot 2x=2x\\sqrt{(1+{x}^{2})}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}} & =\\sqrt{1+{[2x\\sqrt{(1+{x}^{2})}]}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+4{x}^{2}+4{x}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2{x}^{2}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}=2{x}^{2}+1$ to the formula for the arc length, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(2{x}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}+x)|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =[\\frac{2}{3}(3)^{3}+(3)]-[\\frac{2}{3}(0)^{3}+(0)] \\\\  & =21.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-122287/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f87bc14d-5e68-5a5e-bec8-f1b5b21c02e8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122287"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122390/selection/836e3d268c75fcc818e644a293d6d2e095e4011b8c685179f5a02132397ccd86" :answer/id #uuid "1a7b8f63-23fe-501e-9400-8597d549cd94" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2-x)+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122390/selection/280a3e2e028ffc5be0407b9e0fce184970be9c0c90cab0d475a30d11fcfaf2ba" :answer/id #uuid "679f5fae-07a3-5117-bed0-8e4af0509409" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4+x)+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122390/selection/ddc8e17a8e2ee1c8814a13dd4dad20f058a5ef0c7849e1a7cc022aa6fe9bf971" :answer/id #uuid "c141f822-aa3a-58bc-bbe3-8a843ae2fe5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122390/selection/203444b20542a8309a0c3da8419b4c669df7a3a6ac1da8e09c22bc8bfebe4888" :answer/id #uuid "60a38630-03f4-548c-b340-4fcde68748db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-x)+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122390/selection/6df5fe0911ab46341fff3cf1e216b6c2254b36185dcf3e92690b44b0112742aa" :answer/id #uuid "e1343e64-0f5d-515c-b7db-f4566253a593" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122390/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8c093e5c-eb32-58ef-8dd8-6dc41b84f5e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122390/selection/836e3d268c75fcc818e644a293d6d2e095e4011b8c685179f5a02132397ccd86" :answer-field/choices ["q-122390/selection/836e3d268c75fcc818e644a293d6d2e095e4011b8c685179f5a02132397ccd86" "q-122390/selection/280a3e2e028ffc5be0407b9e0fce184970be9c0c90cab0d475a30d11fcfaf2ba" "q-122390/selection/ddc8e17a8e2ee1c8814a13dd4dad20f058a5ef0c7849e1a7cc022aa6fe9bf971" "q-122390/selection/203444b20542a8309a0c3da8419b4c669df7a3a6ac1da8e09c22bc8bfebe4888" "q-122390/selection/6df5fe0911ab46341fff3cf1e216b6c2254b36185dcf3e92690b44b0112742aa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122390" :question/id #uuid "e86eee2a-2a36-501d-8092-4b903ca0e024" :question/math-academy-id "q-122390" :question/problem "The length of a curve $y=f(x)$ is given by ${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{(2-x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Which of the following could be  an equation for this curve?" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe're given that \n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{(2-x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nComparing the above with the arc length formula, we see that we must have\n\n$$\n[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}=\\frac{1}{(2-x)^{2}}\\,⟹\\,{f}^{′}(x)=\\pm \\frac{1}{2-x}.\n$$\n\nIntegrating the above equation with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\pm \\int \\frac{1}{2-x}\\text{ d}x \\\\  & =\\pm (-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2-x))+C \\\\  & =∓\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2-x)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, the only one that has the required form is $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2-x)+1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-122390/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55f783c4-25d6-5855-877e-31bed16b12c4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122390"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-362590/field-1/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" :answer/id #uuid "3fc13f5a-ed09-5ff1-9256-88239684e04c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-362590/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8f415c18-c756-5943-a5cc-69a4c8c88243" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-362590/field-1/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" :answer-field/choices ["q-362590/field-1/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-362590" :question/id #uuid "c5d5aa30-754f-54f8-9942-ed35d6ae4d72" :question/math-academy-id "q-362590" :question/problem "Compute the arc length of $y=\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}+\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x$ for $x\\in [0,1].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$L=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}+\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x,$ $a=0,$ and $b=1.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}=-\\frac{1+x}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}} & =\\sqrt{1+{(-\\frac{1+x}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+\\frac{(1+x)^{2}}{1-{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1-{x}^{2}+1+2x+{x}^{2}}{1-{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{2+2x}{1-{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{2(1+x)}{(1-x)(1+x)}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{1-x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{1-x}}$ into the arc length formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{1-x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{1-x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\sqrt{2}\\sqrt{1-x}\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-2\\sqrt{2}\\sqrt{1-1}-(-2\\sqrt{2}\\sqrt{1-0}) \\\\  & =0-(-2\\sqrt{2}) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 